Junior Racing & Sports Risk Analyst

* BetMakers Technology Group
* Junior Racing & Sports Risk Analyst

## Junior Racing & Sports Risk Analyst

****Do you have a passion for racing and sports? Your future career awaits!****

As a Junior Risk Analyst, you will be responsible for client profiling, servicing our Managed Trading Service (MTS) Risk product, and providing data insights to help shape our Trading strategy. You will use trading data to provide analytics and insights to make informed, data-driven recommendations and decisions around price competitiveness and pricing strategies. Previous experience in horse racing trading (both local and international) would be preferred but is not essential for the role. 



This position is based in our Central London office, offering a hybrid work arrangement that allows you to work from home, with travel required to our London Office ****two days per month****. As a requirement of the role, you will need to work flexible hours, including evenings and weekends in accordance with sports and racing events.

****Day-to-day:****

* Ensuring the Risk Management services provided to our MTS clients is the best in-class service;
* Use trading data to provide analytics and insights to make informed, data-driven recommendations and decisions around price competitiveness and pricing strategies;
* Check and update betting markets;
* Manage the live administration of active markets;
* Provide insights and reporting to key stakeholders to a high quality standard within a timely manner;
* Effectively communicate company and management messages throughout the business;
* Provide strategic suggestions and insights to relevant stakeholders;
* Liaise with external and internal stakeholders as required.

****To be successful in the role:****

* An interest in all things sport and racing;
* Strong numerical and analytical skills;
* The ability to draw sound conclusions from data insights;
* Drive to provide excellent products and services;
* High attention to detail and;
* Strong proactive problem-solving and decision-making skills.

****What you'll love about BetMakers:****

* Hybrid work model, we offer the flexibility to suit your needs;
* Highly competitive short term incentive plan, with attractive bonus entitlements;
* Bespoke learning management system;
* Regular social events, team building, and birthday celebrations and;
* Comprehensive EAP.

*****Sounds like you? Don’t miss this opportunity, apply now!*****

**If you’re self-motivated, innovative and thrive working in a fast-paced environment where no two days are the same, this could be the role for you! Apply now by submitting your resume via the apply now link.**

**To learn more about who we are and the work we do, please visit:****www.betmakers.com**

**BetMakers Technology Group is an inclusive employer, committed to providing a safe workforce environment and encouraging applications from candidates of all backgrounds. We value people of all abilities and diversity of culture, faith, gender identity and sexual orientation. We welcome unique contributions and perspectives of all people to ensure our workforce is representative of the world we work with and live in.**

*****BetMakers Technology Group Ltd (ASX: BET)***** **is the leading software development company for sports and racing solutions with a global footprint. With an ambitious vision and offices across the globe, BetMakers Technology Group is a technology and data partner for some of the world's most recognised and respected bookmakers and rights holders. We design and develop leading edge odds comparisons and intelligent betting platforms, as well as analytics and trading solutions.** **As industry leaders, with our customers at front of mind, we pride ourselves on our passionate and innovative culture. If you're ready to take your career to new heights apply now!**

## Junior Business Analyst – Private Markets Platform

Apply

:   London, United Kingdom

:   Full time

:   Posted Yesterday

:   JR2018

**Job Description**

We are looking for a highly motivated Junior Business Analyst in our fast-growing Private Markets Platform team. The team brings together expertise in Business Analysis, Business Architecture, and Project Management, and plays a central role in shaping how the firm operates at scale. Our focus is on driving large-scale transformations, improving end-to-end processes, and designing scalable, future-ready solutions that support our clients and investment teams.

**What you will do** 

* Designing, re-engineering and documenting key business processes with different stakeholders on business and IT side;
* Conducting requirement analysis and detailed gap assessments on a wide range of topics across the company;
* Writing test cases, organise and perform User Acceptance Testing (UAT);
* Supporting in project management activities, such as organising workshops with SMEs, overseeing IT delivery, preparing status reports and resource & work planning;
* Defining and presenting conceptual approaches (orally and in writing), target operating models, preparing solution options and required decisions, and documenting results;
* Closely working with IT counterparts to bridge between business and technology teams;
* Training business users on rolled-out tools, push for adoption and support the entire change management process.



We are looking for individuals who:  

* Are curious and intellectually engaged, with a genuine interest in understanding complex and evolving business models;
* Naturally ask “why”, challenge assumptions, and seek to understand root causes rather than symptoms;
* Are comfortable challenging the status quo in a constructive and thoughtful way;
* Have a strong desire to learn quickly, especially in new and unfamiliar domains and  take ownership.

**Requirements**

* University degree or equivalent, qualifying experience in Business Economics, Business Informatics or Information Technology;
* First working experience of business analysis in a financial services company or with a leading consulting firm in a similar hands-on role at the interface between Business and IT;
* Motivation to work on own initiative and in collaboration with various stakeholders, ability to deliver on time with a high level of integrity;
* Strong analytical and problem-solving skills, with the ability to understand business and technical functions as well as process information quickly;
* Must be comfortable with constructively challenging the status quo and looking for new ways to improve processes and results;
* Great team player and ability to work collaboratively at various levels of the organization;
* Excellent communication and presentation skills in written and verbal English.

**Contact Information**

If you are interested in becoming an integral part of a successful alternative investment management team in an international, multicultural working environment we will be pleased to get to know you soon.  
For further information please contact us.

Aline de Montmollin

Human Resources

LGT Capital Partners (U.K.) Ltd.

Contact:

+41 58 261 81 60

### About Us

***LGT Capital Partners is a leading global specialist in alternative investing with over USD 110 billion in assets under management and more than 700 institutional clients in 50 countries. An international team of over 900 professionals is responsible for managing a wide range of investment programs focusing on private markets, multi-alternatives and diversifying strategies, as well as sustainable and impact strategies. Headquartered in Pfaeffikon (SZ), Switzerland, the firm has offices in San Francisco, New York, Dublin, London, Paris, The Hague, Luxembourg, Frankfurt am Main, Vaduz, Dubai, Beijing, Hong Kong, Tokyo, Singapore and Sydney.***

# Underwriter, Property and Casualty

**Standort** Birmingham, Vereinigtes Königreich
**Art der Arbeit** Vollzeit
**Arbeitsform** Hybrid
**Job level** Berufserfahrene
**Job ID** 14607
**Unternehmen** Munich Re Specialty - Global Markets
**Anstellungsart** Unbefristet
**Fachbereich** Schadenbearbeitung und Underwriting

Jetzt bewerben

**All locations** Birmingham, Vereinigtes Königreich; Leeds, Vereinigtes Königreich; 

About us

At Munich Re Specialty – Global Markets (MRS-GM), it is our ambition to become the leading Primary Specialty Insurance provider, underpinned by an effective and adaptable strategy, superior products and industry leaders working in a supportive environment to achieve this.

At the heart of our success is a strong culture where people are encouraged to be present, bold and curious, allowing them to achieve their individual goals.

Please see our website for more information.

Underwriter, Property and Casualty

We are currently looking for an Underwriter, Property and Casualty, to be based in either Birmingham or Leeds on a full-time basis, reporting into the P&C Underwriting Manager.

In this role, you will contribute to the underwriting team’s achievement of profitable growth while ensuring the maintenance of a high-quality portfolio across Property & Casualty products, including combined, mono-line, and scheme offerings.

Responsibilities:

**Underwriting**

* Underwrite new and renewal business for allocated intermediaries and customers in line with guidelines, risk appetite, and delegated authority; manage end-to-end underwriting of cases to deliver agreed business development plans aligned with the Company’s trading strategy;
* Make timely, effective underwriting decisions within delegated authority, referring complex risks as appropriate; support underwriting of complex or multinational accounts by contributing tailored solutions;
* Collaborate closely with senior underwriters and key stakeholders within the UK regional business to ensure consistent underwriting processes;
* Plan and manage own workload efficiently to meet customer service standards and credit control targets; contribute to building and managing a profitable, balanced, and sustainable portfolio;
* Continuously develop technical underwriting knowledge and skills through training, mentoring, and practical experience;
* Undertake other duties appropriate to the role level as required.

**Strategic Contribution**

* Identify and develop business opportunities within the allocated portfolio, collaborating with colleagues to ensure efficient business handling;
* Support cross-selling and account development initiatives by working with other lines of business;
* Contribute to maintaining a balanced, high-quality portfolio and promote Munich Re P&C products.

**Technical Expertise**

* Maintain and enhance technical underwriting knowledge across relevant lines of business; deliver technical input and presentations as required;
* Ensure consistent application of underwriting standards and guidelines across the portfolio;
* Promote good Conduct practices and understand escalation processes and governance related to Conduct Risk and underwriting committees.

**Intermediary and Customer Management**

* Develop and maintain effective working relationships with allocated intermediaries and customers, balancing their needs with the Company’s trading objectives;
* Represent Munich Re Global Markets UK in meetings with intermediaries and internal group stakeholders as appropriate;
* Act as a key contact for the allocated intermediaries/customers, supporting business development efforts and maintaining high levels of customer service.

Knowledge and Skills

* Demonstrate a high level of underwriting knowledge, with experience in Real Estate considered advantageous;
* Possess a solid understanding of technical underwriting principles, company philosophy, and trading strategy;
* Ability to interpret and effectively utilize management information to support decision-making;
* Exhibit excellent communication skills to engage effectively with internal and external stakeholders;
* Maintain strong knowledge of the local market dynamics;
* Build and sustain collaborative internal relationships with Line of Business Managers, team members, underwriters, the Claims Department, and the Syndicate;
* Develop and manage external relationships with a diverse range of contacts within allocated intermediaries and customers.

If you are excited about this role but your experience does not align perfectly with everything outlined, or you don’t meet every requirement, we encourage you to apply anyway. You might just be the candidate we are looking for!

Diversity, Equity & Inclusion

At Munich Re, Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion foster innovation and resilience and enable us to act braver and better. Embracing the power of DEI is at the core of who we are. We recognise diversity can be multi-dimensional, intersectional, and complex, so we want to build a diverse workforce that includes a wide range of racial, ethnic, sexual, and gender identities; economic and geographic backgrounds; physical abilities; ages; life, school, and career experiences; and political, religious, and personal beliefs. Additionally, we are committed to building an equitable and inclusive work environment where this diversity is celebrated, valued, and has equitable opportunities to succeed.

All candidates in consideration for any role can request a reasonable adjustment at any point in our recruitment process. You can request an adjustment by speaking to your Talent Acquisition contact.

Learning and innovating today, striving for sustainable societies and business tomorrow

At Munich Re Specialty – Global Markets our approach to sustainability is underpinned by our desire to seize business opportunities and to nurture a stimulating and inclusive work environment. Our sustainability strategy aims to deliver holistic impacts across environmental, social and governance topics.

Learn more about sustainability at Munich Re – choose your impact!

Role Description: A Production Operative will work within any area of Operations, supporting the project and flow sides of the business as required in line with business requirements. Essential Duties (not exhaustive): Ensure their own and the safety of their fellow team members is a priority;
Work to any defined health and safety requirements within the area and support any safety-led initiatives;
Assembly of mechanical metalwork;
Assembly of product components;
Preparation and termination of wiring; Able to read from and work from electrical schematic drawing; Work to defined standard work requirements;
Pack equipment as instructed using the best methods available; Adhere to all quality standards defined and required;
Proactively support Continuous Improvement initiatives; Any other reasonable duty as required and in line with business needs; Assemble various sub-assemblies for production; Inspection of parts for use on production; Flexible approach to tasks given in a busy working environment; Work to set timescales and achieve deadlines; Work efficiently and effectively as part of a team; Maintain a clean and tidy working area; Adhere to all PPE / work wear requirements.
